# GFP-61: pins db_script/init/0001_GFP-9.ddl as a FROZEN baseline (GFP-60).
#
# Deliberately NOT stored inside init/ itself: GFP-61 also asserts init/
# contains exactly one file (the frozen baseline), so a checksum sidecar
# has to live here instead, next to db_script/README.md and
# db_script/schema_snapshot.txt.
#
# tests/test_schema_guard.py fails CI if db_script/init/0001_GFP-9.ddl's
# hash drifts from the one below -- see db_script/README.md ("init/ is
# FROZEN -- do not fold changes back into it") for why that file must never
# change: every change since GFP-60 belongs in db_script/migration/
# instead, so a fresh database is always "init + every migration replayed",
# which is what makes a migration failure always a real failure.
#
# GFP-117 -- THE HASH BELOW IS TAKEN WITH LINE ENDINGS NORMALISED, CRLF and
# lone CR both folded to LF, exactly as grocery_planner/db.py._checksum does
# it. The previous value was a byte-exact hash of a CRLF checkout, so it
# matched only on working copies old enough to predate .gitattributes (added
# by GFP-98, which marks *.ddl as text with LF endings) and failed on every
# fresh clone, every git worktree and every CI runner. Normalised, the value
# is identical either way, which is the whole point.
#
# If you are deliberately re-baselining init/ (this should be exceedingly
# rare -- read the README section above first), regenerate the hash with:
#
#   .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/pin_init_baseline.py
#
# That script exists because the instruction here used to be an inline
# python -c one-liner containing backslash escapes, and pasting it into this
# comment wrote real control characters that split the line and corrupted the
# file. A script cannot be mangled by being quoted.
edb9404ff47028fa6f98e76c6925373ebfdd10429ed9acbb4571fc4d079ee908  init/0001_GFP-9.ddl
